FerrionOS change to upstream base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f with the patches before it in the recipe's list applied.

NvmeCompQueue::complete read the entire 16-byte #[repr(C, packed)] NvmeComp entry with ptr::read_volatile before testing the phase bit in entry.status. Disassembly of the release nvmed binary showed six separate volatile loads in field order, loading cid (offset 0x0c) before status (offset 0x0e). When a controller DMA write of a new completion entry landed between those loads, nvmed observed the new phase bit paired with the previous wrap's cid and sq_head, causing the free-ID guard to drop the real completion and strand its waiter in futex wait (or, before unique command IDs, waking the wrong command). Read the 2-byte aligned status field first with ptr::read_volatile, verify alignment, check the phase bit, issue an Acquire fence, and only then read the full completion entry.

